5,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Welcome, everyone. As we deliberate, let us remember that while funding is essential, the true heart of research lies in the skilled hands that carry it out. We must ensure the chosen project is operationally viable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Sakura,,"I agree! But ""viable"" can be tricky, right? I want to know if the money actually covers everything or if some costs are hidden. Let's make sure the winners aren't surprised by bills later!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think Sakura is right. But maybe we should also look at whether these kinds of projects actually finish on time? I worry about picking something that looks great but just... stalls.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Takumi,,"I'm with Daisuke. It's not just about the money; it's about what stops the work. We need to know where the real interruptions happen before we commit, or we're just wasting time.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree. We must consider the shared infrastructure. If the facilities are already at capacity, even a well-funded project will fail. We should investigate the current state of our shared services and technical staffing.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"Wisdom suggests we look beyond the blueprints. To ensure the project's soul—its people—is intact, I believe we should examine the staffing rolls for technical posts and the minutes on secondments and crew strength.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"That sounds like a plan, Servas! I'm super curious about the money part, so I want to check the travel and bench-fee lines in the ledgers and the national computing agreement and facility day rates!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... if it's okay with everyone, I'd like to look at the closeout files of finished awards and the portfolio review of schedule overruns. I just want to see what actually worked in the past.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Takumi,,I'll take the incident logs on shared instrumentation and the station records from partner field sites. I want to see exactly what breaks or fails in the field and the lab.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Minako,,"I will look into the accreditation and bookings at shared facilities, as well as the national repository deposit turnaround. This will help us determine if the infrastructure can handle additional load.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have a comprehensive plan. By examining both the human element and the physical infrastructure, we ensure that our decision is grounded in reality rather than just ambition. I am content with these choices.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We're like a team of detectives now! I can't wait to see if there are any secret costs hiding in those ledgers. This is going to be so exciting!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope this is the right way to do it. I just don't want us to make a mistake by trusting a flashy proposal that might not actually deliver anything in the end.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"Stop worrying, Daisuke. We're doing the right thing by digging into the dirt first. If there are hidden traps that'll kill the project, I'm going to find them. Let's just get to it.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Minako,,"The division of labor is clear and logical. By covering financial, historical, technical, and infrastructural data, we will have a complete picture of the operational risks. I believe this is the most prudent approach.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us proceed with a spirit of openness and curiosity. I look forward to hearing what each of you discovers, for it is in the sharing of knowledge that we find the clearest path forward.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready! Let's go find all those clues! I'll be the best detective ever and make sure we find every single hidden cost. See you all in a bit!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll... I'll do my best to find something useful. I just hope the past can tell us how to avoid the same mistakes. I'm looking forward to seeing what you all find.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Takumi,,Enough talking. Let's just get the data and see who's actually capable of finishing their work without everything falling apart. I'm ready to see what's really going on behind the scenes.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. Let us move to the investigation phase. I will analyze the facility data and report back on whether the current capacity can realistically support a new high-impact project.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
