60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at these paths, Candidate D is a dream without a home, for the glasshouses are full. Candidate B relies on spectroscopy, which we know is fragile. We must seek a more stable foundation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, you're right! Candidate D is out because of the glasshouses. And Candidate C sounds like it needs those expensive animal costs and phenotyping hands we're missing. I'm leaning towards A or B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate A is the safest choice. It's a catalogue project, which I found usually provides lasting value, and it avoids the breeding colony risks that cause so many delays.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Daisuke, I'm with you. Candidate A is the only one that doesn't rely on a single point of failure. B needs that broken spectroscopy suite, and D is impossible. A is the way to go.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,I agree. Candidate D is impossible due to glasshouse capacity. Candidate B is too risky given the instrumentation failures. Candidate A leverages the efficient national repository and avoids the current infrastructure bottlenecks. It is the most viable choice.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such consensus. Candidate A does not require the vanished phenotyping hands, nor does it depend on the fragile tools of Candidate B. It is a path paved with stability and wisdom.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"Plus, Candidate A is a budget win! It uses the free computing for all those sequences and doesn't need the pricey animal units. It's the perfect choice for our money and our space!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel much better now that we agree. Candidate A builds a resource that others can use for years, and it doesn't seem like it will just stall. I'm happy to support it.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"It's the only one that makes sense. A doesn't depend on a single piece of gear or a specific building. It's robust, and it actually has a chance of finishing. I'm voting for A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,The logic is sound. Candidate A aligns with our available resources and avoids every critical bottleneck we identified. It is the only proposal that is operationally realistic. I also vote for Candidate A.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, when the path is clear and the consensus is rooted in the well-being of the project's future, there is peace in the decision. I shall cast my vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Me too! Candidate A is the smartest pick for the budget and the facilities. It's a total win-win! I'm voting for Candidate A!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll vote for Candidate A too. It's the most reliable way to ensure we actually deliver something of lasting value. I'm glad we could all agree on this.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"No more debating. We've looked at the facts, and A is the only one that won't crash and burn. I'm voting for Candidate A.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
